_n('''(vi) If the interviewer makes a joke, smile to acknowledge that he made one, even if it was not funny.'''),
_n('''(vii) Make sure you have understood the question. If you do not, ask him to clarify it.'''),
_s('''Don'ts:'''),
_n('''(viii) Don't chew gum during the interview.'''),
_n('''(ix) Don't discuss personal problems.'''),
_n('''(x) Do not smoke, even if the interviewer does and offers you a cigarette.'''),
_n('''(xi) Don't interrupt when the interviewer is talking.'''),
_n('''(xii) Don't address the interviewer by his/her first name unless invited to do so.'''),
_n('''(xiii) Don't speak or act in a nervous manner.'''),
_s('''Don't:'''),
_n('''1. Rub the back of your head or neck. Even if you really do just have a cramp in your neck, these gestures make you look disinterested.'''),
_n('''2. Rub or touch your nose. This suggests that you're not being completely honest, and it's gross.'''),
_n('''3. Sit with your arms folded across your chest. You'll appear unfriendly and disengaged.'''),
_n('''4. Cross your legs and idly shake one over the other. It's distracting and shows how uncomfortable you are.'''),
_n('''5. Lean your body towards the door. You'll appear ready to make a mad dash for the door.'''),
_n('''6. Slouch back in your seat. This will make you appear disinterested and unprepared.'''),
_n('''7. Stare back blankly. This is a look people naturally adapt when they are trying to distance themselves.'''),
_s('''Do:'''),
_n('''8. Sit up straight, and lean slightly forward in your chair. In addition to projecting interest and engagement in the interaction, aligning your body's position to that of the interviewer's shows admiration and agreement.'''),
_n('''9. Show your enthusiasm by keeping an interested expression. Nod and make positive gestures in moderation to avoid looking like a bobblehead.'''),
_n('''10. Establish a comfortable amount of personal space between you and the interviewer.'''),
_n('''11. If you have more than one person interviewing you at once, make sure you briefly address both people with your gaze (without looking like a tennis spectator) and return your attention to the person who has asked you a question.'''),
